    <code code="10154-3" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Chief complaint Narrative - Reported"/>
    <title>Chief Complaint</title>
    <text><paragraph>Tooth pain and swelling of the lower right jaw for two days. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Ms. Holiday asked for a same-day visit for pain in a lower right back tooth. The tooth has been sensitive for weeks; two days ago it became a constant throbbing pain, and since yesterday the gum beside it has been swollen. The pain kept her awake last night and is worse with chewing and hot drinks. She felt warm last night but has had no chills. She can open her mouth fully and swallow normally, and she has no swelling under the tongue or down the neck and no trouble breathing. Her dental appointment is still three weeks away. She has taken her usual buprenorphine 16 mg each morning and no other medicine. She came in because she was frightened that the pain would push her toward heroin or toward drinking to get through a show this weekend; she has used neither and called her peer recovery coach last night. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Onset</td><td>Sensitivity for weeks; constant pain for two days</td></tr><tr><td>Location</td><td>Lower right back tooth and the gum beside it</td></tr><tr><td>Duration</td><td>Two days of constant pain; one day of swelling</td></tr><tr><td>Character</td><td>Throbbing</td></tr><tr><td>Severity</td><td>8 of 10 at worst; kept her awake</td></tr><tr><td>Timing</td><td>Constant, worse with chewing</td></tr><tr><td>Context</td><td>Untreated decay found at the preventive visit; dental appointment pending</td></tr><tr><td>Modifying factors</td><td>Worse with chewing and hot drinks; no medicine taken besides her buprenorphine</td></tr><tr><td>Associated signs and symptoms</td><td>Felt warm last night; no chills, trouble opening the mouth, trouble swallowing, neck swelling, or breathlessness. Worried about cravings; no opioid or alcohol use</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

